<title>USA: Spain says committed to join EMU in 1999.</title>
<headline>Spain says committed to join EMU in 1999.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato reiterated on Wednesday that Spain was determined to join European Economic and Monetary Union at the start in 1999.</p>
<p>The economic policies being implemented in Spain were fully in line with meeting Maastricht treaty criteria for entry into monetary union, he told the annual meeting of the International Monetary Fund and World Bank.</p>
<p>&quot;My government is firmly pledged to ensure Spain switches to the euro from the start,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The economic policies being followed were needed not just to meet Maastricht treaty standards but to set Spain on the path of sustained, employment-generating growth.</p>
</text>
